   "source": [
    "<div style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; color: #1e293b; max-width: 900px; background-color: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 10px; padding: 20px; margin-top: 15px; box-sizing: border-box;\">\n",
    "  <!-- SECTION TITLE -->\n",
    "  <div style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; color: #0f172a; margin-bottom: 14px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;\">\n",
    "    Out-of-Sample Predictor Performance & Spatial Tail-Risk Hotspots\n",
    "  </div>\n",
    "  <!-- PANEL DESCRIPTIONS -->\n",
    "  <div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.55; margin-bottom: 18px;\">\n",
    "    <div style=\"background: #ffffff; padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 6px; border-left: 3px solid #2563eb; box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.03);\">\n",
    "      <strong style=\"color: #1e40af;\">Panel A (Predictive Fidelity):</strong> District-level out-of-sample ensemble $R^2$ ($N \\ge 5$), adjusted for local sample size. Darker contours isolate regions where localized variance is structurally predictable rather than noise-dominated.\n",
    "    </div>\n",
    "    <div style=\"background: #ffffff; padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 6px; border-left: 3px solid #d97706; box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.03);\">\n",
    "      <strong style=\"color: #92400e;\">Panel B (Downside Uncertainty):</strong> District-mean width of the 90% conditional quantile prediction interval ($q_{95} - q_{05}$). Darker hues highlight structural volatility hotspots acutely exposed to climate-induced tail losses.\n",
    "    </div>\n",
    "  </div>\n",
    "  <!-- TWO-COLUMN STAKES & STAKEHOLDERS -->\n",
    "  <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 14px; flex-wrap: wrap;\">\n",
    "    <!-- COLUMN 1: THE STAKES -->\n",
    "    <div style=\"flex: 1; min-width: 280px; background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 8px; padding: 14px;\">\n",
    "      <div style=\"font-weight: 700; font-size: 13px; color: #0f172a; margin-bottom: 8px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.4px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;\">\n",
    "        <span> </span> The Analytical Stakes\n",
    "      </div>\n",
    "      <ul style=\"margin: 0; padding-left: 18px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; color: #334155;\">\n",
    "        <li style=\"margin-bottom: 6px;\"><b>Decoupling Skill from Noise:</b> Disentangles pure model capability from intrinsic environmental volatility.</li>\n",
    "        <li style=\"margin-bottom: 6px;\"><b>Adverse Selection & Mispricing:</b> Prevents systemic risk mispricing caused by applying uniform, aggregated regional loss metrics.</li>\n",
    "        <li><b>Tail-Risk Isolation:</b> Pinpoints exact geographies where severe climate anomalies induce heavy-tailed yield variance.</li>\n",
    "      </ul>\n",
    "    </div>\n",
    "    <!-- COLUMN 2: STAKEHOLDER IMPLICATIONS -->\n",
    "    <div style=\"flex: 1; min-width: 280px; background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 8px; padding: 14px;\">\n",
    "      <div style=\"font-weight: 700; font-size: 13px; color: #0f172a; margin-bottom: 8px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.4px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;\">\n",
    "        <span> </span> Stakeholder Implications\n",
    "      </div>\n",
    "      <ul style=\"margin: 0; padding-left: 18px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; color: #334155;\">\n",
    "        <li style=\"margin-bottom: 6px;\"><b>Insurers & Reinsurers:</b> High-fidelity, low-variance zones anchor standard indemnity; high-uncertainty hotspots trigger parametric trigger design.</li>\n",
    "        <li style=\"margin-bottom: 6px;\"><b>Agricultural Lenders:</b> Informs dynamic, risk-adjusted capital buffer requirements and targeted credit facility pricing.</li>\n",
    "        <li><b>Policymakers:</b> Directs adaptation subsidies, resilience infrastructure, and social safety nets to structural risk zones.</li>\n",
    "      </ul>\n",
    "    </div>\n",
    "  </div>\n",
    "</div>"
   ]
